{{Information
|description={{en|1=Hindu devotees dance as they take part in a festival called Lal Kach (Red Glass) during the last day of the Bangla month in Munshigonj, outbreak in Dhaka, Bangladesh on April 13, 2022. The festival is well known for the local community for more than hundred years. The Hindu youth and men paint themselves with red color and attend a procession holding swords as they show power against evil and welcome the Bengali New Year 1428.}}{{ig|1=Ndị na-efe chi n’okpukpe Hindu na-agba egwu ka ha na-ekere òkè n’emume a na-akpọ Lal Kach (Iko Uhie) n’ụbọchị ikpeazụ nke ọnwa Bangla na Munshigonj, dị na mpaghara Dhaka, Bangladesh, na Eprel 13, 2022. Ndị obodo ahụ amarala emume a kemgbe ihe karịrị otu narị afọ. Ndị ntorobịa na ụmụ nwoke Hindu na-ete ahụ ha agba uhie ma sonye n’usoro ngagharị, na-ebu mma agha iji gosi ike ha megide ajọ ihe na ịnabata Afọ Ọhụrụ nke ndị Bengali nke afọ 1428.}}
